{
  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200 → acc 0.520), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical design question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit over RNA alone. Config_014 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, no aggregation, concat) is the most direct extension of the baseline: it keeps the RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and profile setting (singleprofile) identical, and adds the simplest image pipeline (resnet50 + concat fusion, no aggregation). This isolates the effect of introducing the image modality with minimal confounding changes. If performance improves, it justifies further exploration of image encoders, aggregation, and fusion; if it does not, it redirects budget toward RNA-side or profile-setting optimizations. No other available config tests the modality question as cleanly while changing the fewest other parameters."
}

